==Explanation==
The Cat God is a feature that allows you to use four different '''miracles''' during [[battle]]. He doesn't take up any slots in a team, and the miracles all have powerful effects that can change the outcome of a battle drastically. The first miracle the player can use is a free Baby Boom; any subsequent miracles cost [[Cat Food]], so it's only recommended to use him as a total last resort; otherwise, he shouldn't be used at all. However, clearing [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1 unlocks a permanent 70% discount on all miracles.

Powers like '''Baby Boom''' and '''God Bless You''' are most helpful for Cats of the Cosmos Chapters 2 & 3, as they cost very little and help counter the heavily buffed [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] enemies found in the later stages. Using '''Baby Boom''' in these chapters costs less than using a continue and, if used correctly, can almost guarantee victory.

The Cat God is not available to use in [[Zombie Outbreaks]], [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)|The Big Bang]], [[The Aku Realms]], [[Legend Stages]] or the [[Catclaw Dojo]].

==Strategy/Usage for Miracles==
*Only use miracles if you're sure you're going to win after using them. If you mess up afterward, force closing the game will allow you to continue the stage from the point you used your blessing.
*Only use miracles if you have a guaranteed chance of getting the Treasure after the run using the miracle (i.e., you have a Treasure Radar equipped). If you beat the stage but don't get the Treasure, you should use a gold CPU combined with a Treasure Radar to get the treasure, or else it will effectively be wasted.
*Don't use any miracles before the discount you get after Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 1. This is for two reasons: stages before then are usually easy enough to do without buying miracles, and the prices for miracles are quite high. The exception is for the free Baby Boom, which should be saved for a level that might otherwise be too difficult to clear without.

'''Wrath of God'''
* Call down lightning which damages all enemies.
**Ignores Metal enemies' resistance.
*It is not recommended to use this on non-Metal enemies due to its negligible damage.

'''God Bless You'''
*If the enemies are too close to your base, use it to push them back to their base.
*After using it, spam meatshields right away so the enemies don't walk right back to your base.

'''Healing Oasis'''
*Use it when an important unit is about to die.
*This miracle is mainly good for tankers, in addition to fully healing your base.
*This miracle is quite cheap, even before the cost decrease.

'''Baby Boom'''
*Pretty expensive, even after the cost decrease.
*Use it to guarantee a win on a hard stage, preferably combined with a Treasure Radar.
*Costs less than continuing a stage and usually has the same result.
*Best used alongside an active [[Speed Up]], as its timer scales on real time, therefore allowing Speed Up to indirectly prolong its duration.

