==Trivia==
*The Cat God's "idle state" consisting of just his hair and silhouetted face could be a visual pun on 神 (god) and 髪 (hair), both of which can be read as ''kami''.
*The Cat God's body is taken from Adam from "[[wikipedia:The Creation of Adam|The Creation of Adam]]" by [[wikipedia:Michelangelo|Michelangelo]].
*Prior to [[Version 10.7 Update|version 10.7]], the [[music]] that played in The Cat God's menu was the beginning segment of Carl Orff's "''Carmina Burana: '''O Fortuna'''''", which would also play in the [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone]], [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent]], [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed]] and [[Crazed Cats (origin)#Manic Cats|Maniac]] stages. This was likely changed due to copyright.
*According to the [[Legend Stages/OPED|English Stories of Legend opening]], The Cat God is a millennial. He cannot be used in [[Legend Stages]] because they take place before he was born.
**The [[Legend Stages/OPED (Old)|pre-15.4 English Stories of Legend opening]] said he was around '''20''' years old.
***He used to be '''17''' in older versions.
**The [[Legend Stages/OPED|Japanese Stories of Legend opening]] states that he was born sometime during the [[:wikipedia:Heisei era|Heisei era]].
**Despite this, he still appears as an enemy in a Legend Stage, specifically [[Crimes Against the Cosmos]] as [[The Cat God]].
**Despite being introduced in Stories of Legend, [[Cala Maria]]'s English description claims it being sent as a test of faith sent by the Cat God.
*The Cat God was originally named '''God''' in the [[Upgrade Menu]]. This was changed at an unknown date.
*The Cat God is also referred to as '''God''', '''Cat God''', '''Catgod''', '''Cat-God''' and '''God Cat''' at various points throughout the game.
*[[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] is troubled because Cat God keeps hitting on her. Additionally, her Japanese description claims God bestowed her with the Meownir.
**True Valkyrie Cat's description in the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English version]] instead reveals God was sexually harassing her.
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Miko Mitama]] and the temporary [[Gamatoto Expedition|Gamatoto]] helper summoned by the [[Cat Shrine]], Inari, are mentioned as Cat God's loyal servants.
*One of the possible endings for Gamatoto Expedition log messages is "with the Cat God."
*One of the possible Cat Shrine level-up dialogues is "Why does Cat God need XP, anyhow?", and some of the possible Cat Fortunes are "Count 3 shooting stars for Cat God's favor." and "Don't worry just leave it to Cat God."
*In the Battle Cats [https://youtu.be/_4QZsEwPRog official launch trailer], The Cat God appears with lightning strikes right after an [[Assassin Bear]] and [[Shy Boy]] begin to demolish the Cat Army.
*He is the only character in the [[Upgrade Menu]] who cannot be sent out in battle nor increase the player's [[User Rank]].

